    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch03-section-2-3",
      "sourceStart": 10054,
      "sourceEnd": 10070,
      "original": "### 2.3. Duality",
      "action": "moved-to-section-title"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch03-block-0038",
      "sourceStart": 10070,
      "sourceEnd": 10072,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch03-item-2-3-1",
      "sourceStart": 10072,
      "sourceEnd": 10198,
      "original": "#### 2.3.1. Let $v_1,\\ldots,v_n$ be a basis of $V$ and $\\varphi_1,\\ldots,\\varphi_n$ be the dual basis. Then for each $v\\in V$,",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch03-block-0039",
      "sourceStart": 10198,
      "sourceEnd": 10339,
      "sha256": "a50ecfd5f75dbd399ddfb8094c08e33187390545fe934c8fcf0951e1796c4f18"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch03-item-2-3-2",
      "sourceStart": 10339,
      "sourceEnd": 10387,
      "original": "#### 2.3.2. Suppose $T\\in\\mathcal{L}(U,V)$. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch03-block-0040",
      "sourceStart": 10387,
      "sourceEnd": 10520,
      "sha256": "a7bfd3fdd5edf77aeda63bd3b776040d1f141ec7f6fafac26d45a1b92100e638"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch03-item-2-3-3",
      "sourceStart": 10520,
      "sourceEnd": 10662,
      "original": "#### 2.3.3. Suppose $U$ is a subspace of $V$. Then $U_V^0$ is a subspace of $V'$. If $V$ is finite-dimensional, $\\dim(U_V^0)+\\dim(U)=\\dim(V)$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch03-block-0041",
      "sourceStart": 10662,
      "sourceEnd": 10857,
      "sha256": "4addbd839c024e1530231862d394b861476c7da6a5789c91db910c672f0ceedd"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch03-item-2-3-4",
      "sourceStart": 10857,
      "sourceEnd": 10941,
      "original": "#### 2.3.4. Let $T\\in\\mathcal{L}(V,W)$. Then $\\ker(T')=(\\operatorname{range}T)^0_W$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch03-block-0042",
      "sourceStart": 10941,
      "sourceEnd": 11185,
      "sha256": "8369751b24e884338ec7be1105a7c40f55d8abb665897bbfc990224e9b7a4fe6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch03-item-2-3-5",
      "sourceStart": 11185,
      "sourceEnd": 11280,
      "original": "#### 2.3.5. Let $V,W$ be finite-dimensional vector spaces and let $T\\in \\mathcal{L}(V,W)$. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch03-block-0043",
      "sourceStart": 11280,
      "sourceEnd": 11500,
      "sha256": "6ddd1ab9b5c6ab2a8ccb3605700768c17ad0416b7e6747fe4e109a78bd416855"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch03-item-2-3-6",
      "sourceStart": 11500,
      "sourceEnd": 11823,
      "original": "#### 2.3.6. Let $V,W$ be finite-dimensional vector spaces with dual spaces $V',W'$, and let $T\\in\\mathcal L(V,W)$. Let $\\mathscr{B}=\\{v_1,\\ldots,v_n\\},\\mathscr{B'}=\\{\\varphi_1,\\ldots,\\varphi_n\\}$ and $\\mathscr{C}=\\{w_1,\\ldots,w_m\\},\\mathscr{C'}=\\{\\psi_1,\\ldots,\\psi_m\\}$ be bases and dual bases of $V,W$, respectively. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch03-block-0044",
      "sourceStart": 11823,
      "sourceEnd": 11975,
